WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
Good morning John.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:04.410
So for the first time in a long time, I don't
have anything like super pressing to make

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.410
a video about today.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:09.290
I mean, I got ideas, got plenty of ideas,
but instead of doing one of those things,

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:14.570
I decided to turn this video over to the Nerdfighters
of Facebook and Twitter and Tumblr and Reddit

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:17.610
to decide for me what I would do in this video.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.840
"Pretend to be a crab!"

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.270
Oookay.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.699
Rawwwawraaawaahh.

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:25.119
"Spiderman."

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:27.980
Donald Glover.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:28.980
All the way.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.269
"Show us Lemon and her derpiness!"

00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:34.190
"Talk about throwing paper balls near cats
and their subsequent reactions."

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.110
Felis catus, the domesticated house cat.

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:40.540
Interests include meat pâté, warm things
and strings.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.750
The cat considers the paper ball to be a little
bit like a mice.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:48.070
It moves and skitters and makes noises like
a mice, but is not juicy like a mice.

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:49.070
"Juggling!"

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:51.250
"Nerdy Valentines Day jokes!"

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:57.000
I could never break up with my goalie girlfriend;
she's a keeper.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.010
I have a friend who married a librarian.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:03.070
Instead of giving him a ring at the wedding
ceremony, she just stamped him: "Not for circulation".

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:04.300
Yeah, nup, movin' on!

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.680
"Can you tell us anything about your book?"

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.230
Yeah, I'm thinking about writing a fiction-y
thing.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:11.330
Right now it's about a girl, uh, and a robot
and what it means to be human.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:12.590
"Please play Minecraft!"

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:16.400
This is the Nerdcrafteria Minecraft server
which is always beautiful, but is right now

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.800
decorated for Valentines Day.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.070
Isn't it adorable?

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:24.170
"Don a speedo, cover self in peanut butter/bacon
mixture, talk about Gundam."

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:25.170
No!

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.170
No.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:27.880
"TV recommendations please!"

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:30.680
Agent Carter, Agent Carter, Agent Carter,
Agent Carter, Agent Carter.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:33.900
Andrew asks: "What are some of your favourite
things that likely very few people have heard

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:34.900
of?"

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.080
The animated series Kodocha, Locke and Key
comics, Paolo Bacigalupi, the creations of

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:42.650
Neil Cicierega, the board game Robot Ricochet
and let's go with TheThirdPew.

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:43.970
"Show us your lunch!"

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:44.970
Five Guys!

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:49.030
They have free peanuts, but I have to have
my hamburgers on hot dog buns because I can't

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:50.030
eat sesame seeds.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:52.770
"Make video explaining the Keystone XL Pipeline."

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:57.030
Okay, uh, the Keystone XL is an extension
of the current Keystone Pipeline.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:01.330
It would go all the way from Alberta to Louisiana,
which is a long way.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:05.620
The idea being we could get all the oil from
the Tar Sands down to the ports there where

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:06.820
we could ship it all over the world.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:10.649
I think this is a bad idea; the biggest reason
is that the Tar Sands are the second biggest

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:12.370
sink of carbon in the world.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:14.450
And they're a super inefficient source of
oil.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:19.970
It takes a lot of energy, and thus produces
a lot of carbon dioxide, just to turn it into

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:21.280
a usable product.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.160
So you're creating a ton of carbon dioxide
even before you burn the oil.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.950
Tar Sands are what we call unconventional
oil, and ideally, we will leave all of the

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.610
unconventional oil in the ground.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:35.160
'Cause once we start burning the unconventional
oil, there is so much of it, there's just

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.740
so much and it, that's just game over for
climate change.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:43.000
"Try spinning a staff/baton/sword/stick."

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:50.700
"Draw my life!"

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:54.300
Okay, we've not done that yet.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.300
I'm Hank Green.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:58.130
I live in Montana, where I take up a trivial
amount of space.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:02.190
Montana, on the other hand, is a fairly small
percentage of the Earth.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:06.220
The Earth, meanwhile, is a truly minuscule
amount of space in the solar system which

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:11.250
is likewise basically insignificant compared
to the size of our galaxy which, once again,

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.470
is completely trivial compared to the size
of the known universe.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:18.510
My life will take place during an amount of
time, that is, on a universal scale, not just

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.450
insignificant, but unnoticeable.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:22.450
My life.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:23.450
I drew it.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:24.450
"Make a cover song or a parody!"

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:30.090
[singing a la "Blank Space"] 'Cause it's all
up on my head part, well maybe just the front.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:36.290
Being the owner of it ain't hard, can't think
of what I'd rather want.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:41.819
I've been told it's pretty awesome, better
than a bottle of champagne.

00:03:41.819 --> 00:03:46.890
I got a Hank face baby, and I'll write your
name.

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.280
On my face.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:49.770
I won't actually do that though.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:52.290
Okay, I think that's good; it's probably going
to be about 4 minutes.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:56.240
I'm guessing, but I've been doing this for
a while so I'm probably spot on.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:57.240
We'll see.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:58.279
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

